% The closest published relative of the paper's R2: it derives a context-length
% bound beyond which a fixed attention-score comparison cannot jointly avoid
% "semantic reversal" and positional insensitivity. Cited so the paper's own
% claim - per-feature, per-distance, at all distances - can be distinguished
% from a head-level comparison failure at long context.
